{"name":"Stingray Grey","hex":"#b0aba3","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"stingray","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various large, venomous rays, of the orders Rajiformes and Myliobatiformes, having a barbed, whiplike tail.","A device that simulates a cell tower, used to intercept cell phone communications."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stingray"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Stingray","blocks":[{"text":"Stingrays are a group of rays, a type of cartilaginous fish. They are classified in the suborder Myliobatoidei of the order Myliobatiformes and consist of eleven families: Hexatrygonidae, Gymnuridae, Plesiobatidae, Urolophidae, Myliobatidae, Aetobatidae, Mobulidae, Rhinopteridae, Dasyatidae, Potamotrygonidae, and Urotrygonidae .\nThere are about 220 known stingray species organized into 29 genera."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/SStringray.jpg/330px-SStringray.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stingray","wikidata":"Q5328202"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/com